Package: spotify-ad-muter
Version: @VERSION@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-pulsectl, playerctl
Recommends: spotify-client
Maintainer: Nickychemos <surajit.das0320@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Nickychemos/Spotify-Ad-Muter
Description: Mute Spotify advertisements on Linux
 Detects when Spotify is playing an advertisement via its MPRIS D-Bus
 interface and mutes its PulseAudio/PipeWire output stream until music
 resumes. The ad still plays out, only the sound is muted, so Spotify
 cannot tell that it was skipped.
 .
 Runs as a systemd user service that auto-starts on login. Works only
 with the official spotify-client .deb; the Snap and Flatpak builds
 refuse the MPRIS queries this tool relies on.
